# Application Layer

Use cases (commands & queries) and DTOs — the "what" of the system.

Rules:
- Each use case is a class with a single `execute()` method (or multiple
  query/command methods).
- Use cases depend ONLY on domain interfaces (repository ports) — never on
  concrete implementations.
- DTOs are plain data classes or Pydantic models that define the shape of
  data crossing the application boundary.
- Use cases NEVER import from `infrastructure/`.
- Use cases may import from `domain/` and from `src/errors/`.

Files per bounded context:
- `use_case.py` — commands and queries
- `dto.py` — data transfer objects
